    # Get OAuth connect URL
    # Initiate an OAuth connection flow. Returns an authUrl to redirect the user to.  ### Modes  - Standard flow: Zernio hosts the selection UI, then redirects to your redirect_url. - Headless mode (headless=true): user is redirected to your redirect_url with OAuth data for custom UI. Use the platform-specific selection endpoints to complete.  ### Several accounts per platform  A profile can hold several accounts of the same platform. Connecting a different account adds it as a new account, and reconnecting the SAME account keeps it and all of its history.  Ads connections stay one per profile.  On a legacy plan limited to N profiles, a new account is refused with 403 `platform_account_limit` once N accounts of its platform are connected.  ### TikTok  Every connection now goes through the TikTok for Business app.  An authorization that leaves out a permission the connected account needs changes nothing at all and comes back as `missing_tiktok_permissions`. Connect again and accept every permission on TikTok's screen. 
    # @param platform [String] Social media platform to connect. &#x60;snapchat&#x60; is a closed beta with no public release date: it returns 403 &#x60;PLATFORM_BETA_RESTRICTED&#x60; until the account is approved.
    # @param profile_id [String] Your Zernio profile ID (get from /v1/profiles). For WhatsApp, a Zernio-provisioned number can only be connected on the profile it was provisioned to; connecting from any other profile is rejected with a 409.
    # @param [Hash] opts the optional parameters
    # @option opts [String] :reconnect_account_id Refresh this existing account: a Zernio account id of the same platform on this profile (otherwise 400).  The OAuth callback and the selection endpoints (select-page, select-organization, select-board, select-location, Instagram and Snapchat selection) refuse with &#x60;reconnect_account_mismatch&#x60; a login that would write to a different account of the platform on this profile instead of this one.  In headless mode the marker travels in the redirect_url we hand you, so pass that URL back unchanged to the selection endpoint. On X it counts toward the OAuth state limit described under redirect_url. 
    # @option opts [String] :oauth_app_id Connect through one of your own OAuth apps (see /v1/connect/oauth-apps), so the consent screen shows your app and the platform&#39;s limits are your app&#39;s. Without it the connect runs on Zernio&#39;s app, whatever apps the workspace has saved.  - Only platforms listed in &#x60;platforms&#x60; of GET /v1/connect/oauth-apps accept an app. Any other returns 400, and so do ads connects (&#x60;adsConnect&#x3D;true&#x60; in the redirect URL). - Connects that end on a destination picker also return 400, except Facebook Pages, Google Business locations, Pinterest boards and Snapchat public profiles (Instagram through Facebook Login, for example). - A LinkedIn connect through an app saves the member&#39;s own profile: organization pages, and mention lookups, stay on Zernio&#39;s app. - The connect requests the app&#39;s &#x60;scopeAreas&#x60;. &#x60;scopes&#x60; may narrow them but not add an area the app does not enable (400). - If the user does not grant every requested area, the account still connects and the redirect carries &#x60;missing_permissions&#x3D;&lt;areas&gt;&#x60; (the headless POST returns &#x60;missingPermissions&#x60;). - If the platform refuses a permission your app is not approved for, the redirect carries &#x60;error&#x3D;oauth_app_scope_not_allowed&#x60;.  The account remembers the app, and token refresh, publishing and inbox run on it. Reconnecting through another app, or without one, moves the account to that app. 
    # @option opts [String] :expected_platform_user_id Only connect if the login lands on this platform account. Any other account ends the flow with &#x60;error&#x3D;account_mismatch&#x60; (a 409 &#x60;account_mismatch&#x60; on POST /v1/connect/instagram/select-account) and nothing is written.  Compared with every id the platform reports for the authorized account:  - Any platform: the &#x60;platformUserId&#x60; of a Zernio account on this platform. - Instagram: either the app-scoped id or the professional account id (&#x60;metadata.instagramScopedId&#x60;, the &#x60;17841...&#x60; id that Facebook Login accounts hold as platformUserId). - TikTok: open_ids are app-scoped, so an id from your own TikTok app never matches. Use expectedUsername there.  Honoured by the OAuth callback (every platform that connects without a selection step, Instagram Login included) and by the Instagram selection step. On the other selection endpoints you choose the destination yourself.  In headless mode the marker travels in the redirect_url we hand you, so pass that URL back unchanged. On X it counts toward the OAuth state limit described under redirect_url. 
    # @option opts [String] :expected_username Only connect if the authorized account&#39;s handle is this one (case-insensitive, a leading @ is ignored). Otherwise the flow ends with &#x60;error&#x3D;account_mismatch&#x60; and &#x60;error_message&#x60; naming the handle that was authorized, and nothing is written.  Same coverage and transport as expectedPlatformUserId; when both are sent, both must match. Use this on a first connection, where you hold the handle the user typed but no Zernio id yet. 
    # @option opts [Boolean] :force_reauth Instagram Login only (the default loginMethod); ignored elsewhere. Makes Instagram show its login page and ask for the credentials of the account to connect, even when another Instagram account is logged in on the device or app. Also hides the Facebook login option on that page.  Use it when the person connecting manages several Instagram accounts on one phone: otherwise Instagram logs in, and converts to a professional account, whichever account is active, before any consent screen. Pair it with expectedUsername to also refuse a wrong account at the end.  (default to false)
    # @option opts [String] :redirect_url Your custom redirect URL after the connection completes. It MUST be an absolute http(s) URL or a custom app scheme for mobile deeplinks (e.g. myapp://callback). A relative path is rejected with 400 &#x60;INVALID_REDIRECT_URL&#x60;.  **Exit notice:** when &#x60;redirect_url&#x60; is an http(s) URL on another site (anything but zernio.com), every redirect of the flow lands first on &#x60;https://zernio.com/connect/continue?to&#x3D;&lt;your URL&gt;&#x60;, a Zernio page that names your site and continues to it with one click. All params below reach your URL unchanged.  A custom app scheme (myapp://...) never goes through the notice. In headless mode the redirects we hand you (and the &#x60;redirect_url&#x60; returned by the selection endpoints) are notice URLs: pass them back or navigate to them as they are.  **X (twitter) length limit:** X caps the OAuth &#x60;state&#x60; at 500 characters and the redirect travels inside it (wrapped in the notice URL for an http(s) URL on another site). The URL-encoded form must be at most 258 characters for API callers, 310 for dashboard sessions.  In headless mode the appended &#x60;headless&#x3D;true&#x60; counts toward that limit. A plain https URL on another site leaves about 165 to 190 characters of your own URL, depending on encoding. A longer one is rejected with 400 &#x60;INVALID_REDIRECT_URL&#x60;, and the error says by how much.  **Success params** are appended with the URL API, so an existing query string is preserved:  - Standard mode: connected&#x3D;{platform}&amp;profileId&#x3D;X&amp;accountId&#x3D;Y&amp;username&#x3D;Z. - Headless mode: OAuth data params for platforms requiring selection (e.g. LinkedIn orgs, Facebook pages). If no selection is needed, the account is created directly and the redirect includes accountId.  **Failure params:** the browser goes to the same redirect_url with &#x60;error&#x60; and &#x60;platform&#x60; appended (always present). &#x60;error_message&#x60;, &#x60;is_user_fixable&#x60;, &#x60;reason&#x60;, &#x60;dashboard_url&#x60;, &#x60;missing_scopes&#x60;, &#x60;error_reason&#x60; and the &#x60;platform_error*&#x60; params are conditional: treat them as optional.  Your own query params are kept on every redirect, but ours overwrite one of yours with the same name. On an error redirect we remove the internal &#x60;headless&#x60;, &#x60;adsConnect&#x60;, &#x60;adsScope&#x60;, &#x60;reconnectAccountId&#x60;, &#x60;expectedPlatformUserId&#x60; and &#x60;expectedUsername&#x60; markers added during the flow.  **Correlation** params appear on every redirect from an OAuth callback (success and failure) and on the &#x60;redirect_url&#x60; returned by the selection endpoints such as POST /v1/connect/facebook/select-page:  - &#x60;request_id&#x60;: the id we log that request under. Quote it when reporting a problem. - &#x60;stage&#x60;: where the flow ended. &#x60;authorize&#x60; &#x3D; the platform&#39;s consent dialog returned an error or denial instead of a code. &#x60;callback&#x60; &#x3D; we processed the returned code (success, a selection step, or a failure). - &#x60;stage&#x60; &#x3D; &#x60;select_page&#x60;: the destination-selection endpoint (page, account, organization, board, location, profile or phone number) completed it.  **Error details:**  - &#x60;oauth_denied&#x60;: carries &#x60;error_message&#x60; and, when the platform sent them, its own &#x60;platform_error&#x60; (e.g. &#x60;access_denied&#x60;), &#x60;platform_error_reason&#x60; (e.g. &#x60;user_denied&#x60;) and &#x60;platform_error_description&#x60; (truncated to 500 characters). &#x60;is_user_fixable&#x3D;true&#x60; when the platform reported that the user cancelled or declined. - &#x60;no_facebook_pages&#x60;: comes with &#x60;is_user_fixable&#x3D;true&#x60;, an &#x60;error_message&#x60; telling the user to click \&quot;Edit previous settings\&quot; in Meta&#39;s dialog and tick the Page (or create one), and &#x60;error_reason&#x60; when Meta&#39;s token debug answered (values below). - &#x60;code_already_redeemed&#x60;: the same authorization code arrived more than once and an earlier request already processed it (the code is never sent to the platform twice). Not a failure: check GET /v1/accounts or wait for the &#x60;account.connected&#x60; webhook. - &#x60;missing_google_permissions&#x60; (YouTube, Google Business and Google Ads): the user unchecked permissions on Google&#39;s consent screen. Always with &#x60;is_user_fixable&#x3D;true&#x60;. When Google reported granted scopes, &#x60;missing_scopes&#x60; lists the requested scopes not granted (comma-separated). Ask the user to connect again keeping every permission checked. - &#x60;no_youtube_channel&#x60;: Google authorized the account but it has no YouTube channel we can connect. Always with &#x60;is_user_fixable&#x3D;true&#x60; and an &#x60;error_message&#x60;.  Usual causes of &#x60;no_youtube_channel&#x60;: the user picked their personal Google identity instead of the Brand Account in Google&#39;s account chooser, they only have YouTube Studio access (not Brand Account owner or manager), or the account has no channel yet.  &#x60;error_reason&#x60; values for &#x60;no_facebook_pages&#x60;:  - &#x60;pages_permission_declined&#x60;: the user declined the pages_show_list permission. - &#x60;no_pages_granted&#x60;: the permission was granted with no Page ticked. Meta reports a user who manages no Page the same way, so this covers both. - &#x60;granted_pages_not_listed&#x60;: Pages were ticked but Meta listed none the user can manage, and a direct read of each ticked Page returned no access token.  **Headless &#x60;userProfile&#x60;:** on headless Facebook success (&#x60;step&#x3D;select_page&#x60;) and headless Instagram &#x60;facebook_login&#x60; success (&#x60;step&#x3D;select_account&#x60;), &#x60;userProfile&#x60; is JSON percent-encoded once before being set as a query param, so it is encoded twice on the wire.  After your framework decodes the query string once, run one more decodeURIComponent (or equivalent), then JSON.parse it. &#x60;tempToken&#x60; and &#x60;connect_token&#x60; are plain values.  **Error values.** This list is NOT exhaustive and new values may be added at any time: treat an unrecognized value as a generic failure rather than matching exhaustively. Existing values are not renamed or removed without notice.  - OAuth and callback: &#x60;oauth_denied&#x60;, &#x60;invalid_callback&#x60;, &#x60;invalid_state&#x60;, &#x60;unsupported_platform&#x60;, &#x60;connection_failed&#x60;, &#x60;internal_error&#x60;, &#x60;token_exchange_failed&#x60;, &#x60;byok_config_error&#x60;, &#x60;personal_account_not_supported&#x60;, &#x60;missing_google_permissions&#x60;, &#x60;missing_tiktok_permissions&#x60;, &#x60;platform_requires_destination&#x60;, &#x60;reconnect_account_mismatch&#x60;, &#x60;account_mismatch&#x60;, &#x60;instagram_login_method_mismatch&#x60;, &#x60;invalid_request&#x60;, &#x60;code_already_redeemed&#x60;. - Access and limits: &#x60;profile_not_found&#x60;, &#x60;invalid_profile_id&#x60;, &#x60;access_denied&#x60;, &#x60;account_limit_exceeded&#x60;, &#x60;profile_limit_exceeded&#x60;, &#x60;payment_required&#x60;. - Destination selection: &#x60;no_facebook_pages&#x60;, &#x60;facebook_pages_error&#x60;, &#x60;no_google_locations&#x60;, &#x60;google_locations_error&#x60;, &#x60;google_permission_denied&#x60;, &#x60;no_snapchat_public_profiles&#x60;, &#x60;snapchat_profiles_error&#x60;, &#x60;no_youtube_channel&#x60;, &#x60;discord_no_guild&#x60;, &#x60;slack_no_team&#x60;. - WhatsApp: &#x60;whatsapp_error&#x60;, &#x60;one_whatsapp_per_profile&#x60;, &#x60;whatsapp_number_already_connected&#x60;, &#x60;whatsapp_number_pinned_to_profile&#x60;, &#x60;whatsapp_coexistence_not_registered&#x60;, &#x60;connection_cancelled&#x60;. - Google Ads (platform&#x3D;googleads): &#x60;google_ads_auth_failed&#x60;, &#x60;google_ads_invalid_state&#x60;, &#x60;google_ads_config_error&#x60;, &#x60;google_ads_token_failed&#x60;, &#x60;google_ads_quota_exhausted&#x60;, &#x60;google_ads_callback_error&#x60;. - TikTok Ads (platform&#x3D;tiktokads): &#x60;tiktok_ads_auth_failed&#x60;, &#x60;tiktok_ads_invalid_state&#x60;, &#x60;tiktok_ads_access_denied&#x60;, &#x60;tiktok_ads_config_error&#x60;, &#x60;tiktok_ads_token_failed&#x60;, &#x60;tiktok_ads_account_not_found&#x60;, &#x60;tiktok_ads_callback_error&#x60;. - X Ads (platform&#x3D;xads): &#x60;x_ads_denied&#x60;, &#x60;x_ads_auth_failed&#x60;, &#x60;x_ads_config_error&#x60;, &#x60;x_ads_account_not_found&#x60;, &#x60;x_ads_state_error&#x60;, &#x60;x_ads_token_failed&#x60;, &#x60;x_ads_token_missing&#x60;, &#x60;x_ads_callback_error&#x60;. - Reddit Ads (platform&#x3D;redditads): &#x60;reddit_ads_auth_failed&#x60;, &#x60;reddit_ads_invalid_state&#x60;, &#x60;reddit_ads_access_denied&#x60;, &#x60;reddit_ads_scope_not_granted&#x60;, &#x60;reddit_ads_no_ad_accounts&#x60;, &#x60;reddit_ads_callback_error&#x60;. - Shopify (platform&#x3D;shopify): &#x60;shopify_auth_failed&#x60;, &#x60;shopify_config_error&#x60;, &#x60;shopify_invalid_state&#x60;, &#x60;shopify_invalid_hmac&#x60;, &#x60;shopify_invalid_shop&#x60;, &#x60;shopify_missing_scopes&#x60;, &#x60;shopify_callback_error&#x60;.  Notes:  1. On this endpoint every upstream OAuth error collapses into &#x60;oauth_denied&#x60;, with the provider&#39;s values in the &#x60;platform_error*&#x60; params. The dedicated ads flows differ: they use their own denial slugs, and &#x60;google_ads_auth_failed&#x60; and &#x60;tiktok_ads_auth_failed&#x60; may carry the provider&#39;s raw error string in &#x60;error_message&#x60;. 2. On the tiktok and twitter ads flows &#x60;platform&#x60; carries the ads platform id (&#x60;tiktokads&#x60;, &#x60;xads&#x60;), not the value in the request path. The googleads, redditads and shopify flows report &#x60;googleads&#x60;, &#x60;redditads&#x60; and &#x60;shopify&#x60;. 3. &#x60;missing_tiktok_permissions&#x60;: the TikTok authorization left out a permission the already-connected account needs, so nothing changed and it keeps working as before. User-fixable: connect again and accept every permission on TikTok&#39;s screen. 4. &#x60;instagram_login_method_mismatch&#x60;: an Instagram Login authorization landed on a profile whose Instagram account is connected through Facebook Login, so nothing changed. To refresh it, connect again with &#x60;loginMethod&#x3D;facebook_login&#x60;. To move it to Instagram Login, disconnect it first. 
    # @option opts [String] :scopes Comma-separated permission areas to request instead of the platform&#39;s full permission set.  **Values:** &#x60;posting&#x60;, &#x60;analytics&#x60;, &#x60;comments&#x60;, &#x60;messaging&#x60;, &#x60;ads&#x60;; on google and microsoft, &#x60;email&#x60;, &#x60;calendar&#x60;, &#x60;files&#x60;, &#x60;contacts&#x60;.  **Default:** omit it (what the dashboard does) to request everything the platform supports. Google and microsoft REQUIRE it (400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60; when absent) because their consent screens are reviewed per area.  When present, the consent dialog asks only for the scopes behind those areas, plus the scopes every connection needs (identity, token refresh, listing the pages, organizations or channels the user picks from).  - Scopes never asked for are absent from the account&#39;s &#x60;permissions&#x60;, and the health endpoints report them as not granted. A &#x60;posting&#x60;-only account cannot read analytics or the inbox until reconnected with more areas. - First comments need &#x60;comments&#x60;: a &#x60;posting&#x60;-only account publishes the post and skips the first comment. - Scopes in none of the areas (X likes, bookmarks and follows, Pinterest ads-only extras) are requested only when the parameter is omitted.  **Supported on** facebook, instagram (both login methods), linkedin, twitter, tiktok, youtube, threads, reddit, pinterest, googlebusiness and slack (via &#x60;GET /v1/connect/slack&#x60;).  **Rejected** with 400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60; (&#x60;param: scopes&#x60;) on bluesky, telegram, discord, snapchat and whatsapp (their dialog cannot be reduced), and for an empty list or an unknown area.  What each area asks for, per platform (Google scopes shortened to their last path segment):  | Platform | &#x60;posting&#x60; | &#x60;analytics&#x60; | &#x60;comments&#x60; | &#x60;messaging&#x60; | &#x60;ads&#x60; | Always requested | |---|---|---|---|---|---|---| | facebook | &#x60;pages_manage_posts&#x60; | &#x60;read_insights&#x60;, &#x60;pages_read_user_content&#x60; | &#x60;pages_manage_engagement&#x60;, &#x60;pages_read_user_content&#x60; | &#x60;pages_messaging&#x60; | &#x60;ads_management&#x60;, &#x60;ads_read&#x60;, &#x60;leads_retrieval&#x60;, &#x60;pages_manage_ads&#x60;, &#x60;instagram_basic&#x60;, &#x60;business_management&#x60; | &#x60;pages_show_list&#x60;, &#x60;pages_read_engagement&#x60;, &#x60;pages_manage_metadata&#x60; | | instagram (Instagram Login) | &#x60;instagram_business_content_publish&#x60; | &#x60;instagram_business_manage_insights&#x60; | &#x60;instagram_business_manage_comments&#x60; | &#x60;instagram_business_manage_messages&#x60; | none | &#x60;instagram_business_basic&#x60; | | instagram (&#x60;loginMethod&#x3D;facebook_login&#x60;) | &#x60;instagram_content_publish&#x60; | &#x60;instagram_manage_insights&#x60; | &#x60;instagram_manage_comments&#x60; | &#x60;instagram_manage_messages&#x60; | &#x60;ads_management&#x60;, &#x60;ads_read&#x60;, &#x60;leads_retrieval&#x60;, &#x60;pages_manage_ads&#x60; | &#x60;instagram_basic&#x60;, &#x60;pages_show_list&#x60;, &#x60;pages_read_engagement&#x60;, &#x60;business_management&#x60;, &#x60;pages_messaging&#x60;, &#x60;pages_manage_metadata&#x60; | | linkedin | &#x60;w_member_social&#x60;, &#x60;w_organization_social&#x60;, &#x60;r_organization_social&#x60;, &#x60;r_organization_followers&#x60; | &#x60;r_member_postAnalytics&#x60;, &#x60;r_member_profileAnalytics&#x60;, &#x60;rw_organization_admin&#x60;, &#x60;r_organization_social&#x60;, &#x60;r_organization_followers&#x60; | &#x60;w_member_social&#x60;, &#x60;w_member_social_feed&#x60;, &#x60;w_organization_social&#x60;, &#x60;w_organization_social_feed&#x60;, &#x60;r_organization_social&#x60;, &#x60;r_organization_social_feed&#x60; | none | &#x60;r_ads&#x60;, &#x60;rw_ads&#x60;, &#x60;r_ads_reporting&#x60;, &#x60;r_marketing_leadgen_automation&#x60;, &#x60;rw_conversions&#x60; | &#x60;openid&#x60;, &#x60;profile&#x60;, &#x60;email&#x60;, &#x60;r_basicprofile&#x60;, &#x60;rw_organization_admin&#x60; | | twitter | &#x60;tweet.write&#x60;, &#x60;media.write&#x60; | (in the always-requested set) | &#x60;tweet.write&#x60;, &#x60;like.write&#x60;, &#x60;tweet.moderate.write&#x60; | &#x60;dm.read&#x60;, &#x60;dm.write&#x60;, &#x60;media.write&#x60; | none | &#x60;tweet.read&#x60;, &#x60;users.read&#x60;, &#x60;offline.access&#x60; | | tiktok | &#x60;video.publish&#x60; | &#x60;user.info.stats&#x60;, &#x60;user.insights&#x60;, &#x60;video.list&#x60;, &#x60;video.insights&#x60; | &#x60;comment.list&#x60;, &#x60;comment.list.manage&#x60;, &#x60;video.list&#x60; | &#x60;message.list.read&#x60;, &#x60;message.list.send&#x60;, &#x60;message.list.manage&#x60; | none | &#x60;user.info.basic&#x60;, &#x60;user.info.username&#x60;, &#x60;user.info.profile&#x60;, &#x60;user.account.type&#x60;, &#x60;video.publish&#x60;, &#x60;video.upload&#x60;, &#x60;video.list&#x60; | | youtube | &#x60;youtube.upload&#x60; | &#x60;yt-analytics.readonly&#x60; | &#x60;youtube.force-ssl&#x60; | none | none | &#x60;youtube&#x60; | | threads | &#x60;threads_content_publish&#x60;, &#x60;threads_manage_replies&#x60;, &#x60;threads_delete&#x60; | &#x60;threads_manage_insights&#x60; | &#x60;threads_content_publish&#x60;, &#x60;threads_read_replies&#x60;, &#x60;threads_manage_replies&#x60;, &#x60;threads_delete&#x60; | none | none | &#x60;threads_basic&#x60; | | reddit | &#x60;submit&#x60;, &#x60;read&#x60;, &#x60;mysubreddits&#x60;, &#x60;flair&#x60;, &#x60;history&#x60;, &#x60;edit&#x60; | &#x60;read&#x60;, &#x60;history&#x60; | &#x60;read&#x60;, &#x60;history&#x60;, &#x60;edit&#x60;, &#x60;vote&#x60; | &#x60;privatemessages&#x60; | none | &#x60;identity&#x60; | | pinterest | &#x60;boards:write&#x60;, &#x60;pins:read&#x60;, &#x60;pins:write&#x60; | &#x60;pins:read&#x60;, &#x60;user_accounts:read&#x60; | none | none | &#x60;ads:read&#x60;, &#x60;ads:write&#x60;, &#x60;boards:write&#x60;, &#x60;pins:read&#x60;, &#x60;pins:write&#x60; | &#x60;boards:read&#x60;, &#x60;user_accounts:read&#x60; | | googlebusiness | &#x60;business.manage&#x60; | &#x60;business.manage&#x60; | &#x60;business.manage&#x60; | none | none | &#x60;business.manage&#x60;, &#x60;userinfo.profile&#x60;, &#x60;userinfo.email&#x60; | | slack | &#x60;chat:write&#x60;, &#x60;chat:write.public&#x60;, &#x60;chat:write.customize&#x60;, &#x60;files:write&#x60;, &#x60;files:read&#x60; | none | none | &#x60;chat:write&#x60;, &#x60;chat:write.customize&#x60;, &#x60;files:write&#x60;, &#x60;files:read&#x60;, &#x60;channels:history&#x60;, &#x60;groups:history&#x60;, &#x60;im:history&#x60;, &#x60;mpim:history&#x60;, &#x60;im:read&#x60;, &#x60;im:write&#x60;, &#x60;mpim:read&#x60;, &#x60;users:read&#x60;, &#x60;reactions:read&#x60;, &#x60;reactions:write&#x60; | none | &#x60;channels:join&#x60;, &#x60;channels:read&#x60;, &#x60;groups:read&#x60;, &#x60;team:read&#x60; |  Google and Microsoft accounts use the mailbox areas instead (&#x60;scopes&#x60; is required there):  | Platform | &#x60;email&#x60; | &#x60;calendar&#x60; | &#x60;files&#x60; | &#x60;contacts&#x60; | Always requested | |---|---|---|---|---|---| | google | &#x60;gmail.modify&#x60; | &#x60;calendar&#x60; | &#x60;drive.file&#x60; (only files Zernio created or the user picked, see the Files tag) | &#x60;contacts.readonly&#x60; | &#x60;openid&#x60;, &#x60;userinfo.email&#x60;, &#x60;userinfo.profile&#x60; | | microsoft | &#x60;Mail.ReadWrite&#x60;, &#x60;Mail.Send&#x60; | &#x60;Calendars.ReadWrite&#x60; | &#x60;Files.ReadWrite&#x60; | &#x60;Contacts.Read&#x60; | &#x60;openid&#x60;, &#x60;profile&#x60;, &#x60;email&#x60;, &#x60;offline_access&#x60;, &#x60;User.Read&#x60; |  Areas accumulate: reconnecting with more areas widens the grant, and &#x60;GET /v1/accounts/{accountId}/health&#x60; reports the result. 
    # @option opts [String] :login_hint google and microsoft only: pre-fills the account picker with this address so the user lands on the right mailbox.
    # @option opts [Boolean] :headless When true, the user is redirected to your redirect_url with raw OAuth data (code, state) instead of Zernio&#39;s default account selection UI. Use this to build a custom connect experience. (default to false)
    # @option opts [String] :login_method Instagram only: which of the two Instagram connection methods to use. Ignored for every other platform.  - &#x60;instagram_login&#x60; (default when omitted): the Instagram Login dialog. The user authorizes their Instagram professional account directly, no Facebook Page required. Exception: if omitted and &#x60;reconnectAccountId&#x60; names an account connected with &#x60;facebook_login&#x60;, the reconnect keeps that method. - &#x60;facebook_login&#x60;: the Facebook Login dialog (\&quot;Instagram API with Facebook Login\&quot;). The user authorizes a Facebook Page with a linked Instagram professional account, and every API call for that account runs through the Page. Use it when the customer manages Instagram through a Page and expects the Facebook consent screen.  With &#x60;facebook_login&#x60; the user picks a Page, so the callback continues at the account-selection step, &#x60;/v1/connect/instagram/select-account&#x60;. The default &#x60;instagram_login&#x60; has no selection step and connects directly.  &#x60;facebook_login&#x60; supports &#x60;headless&#x3D;true&#x60; like the other selection platforms. The callback redirects to your &#x60;redirect_url&#x60; with &#x60;profileId&#x60;, &#x60;tempToken&#x60;, &#x60;platform&#x3D;instagram&#x60;, &#x60;step&#x3D;select_account&#x60;, &#x60;userProfile&#x60; and &#x60;connect_token&#x60;.  &#x60;userProfile&#x60; is the Facebook user&#39;s profile, same shape and encoding as the Facebook &#x60;step&#x3D;select_page&#x60; redirect. Pass &#x60;profileId&#x60;, &#x60;tempToken&#x60; and &#x60;connect_token&#x60; into the select-account endpoints to finish.  (default to 'instagram_login')
    # @option opts [String] :onboarding WhatsApp only. Ignored for every other platform. Controls which screen Meta&#39;s Embedded Signup popup shows.  If omitted, the connection defaults to coexistence (same as &#x60;business_app&#x60; below), preserving existing behavior for numbers already on the WhatsApp Business app.  &#x60;api&#x60;: standard Embedded Signup, showing Meta&#39;s WABA/number picker. Use this to connect a phone number already on Cloud API elsewhere.  &#x60;business_app&#x60;: coexistence, i.e. &#39;Connect existing WhatsApp Business app&#39; (a number shared between Cloud API and the consumer WhatsApp Business app). 
    # @option opts [String] :signup WhatsApp only. Rejected with 400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60; on any other platform.  &#x60;hosted&#x60;: &#x60;authUrl&#x60; points at a Zernio-hosted page on zernio.com instead of Meta&#39;s OAuth dialog, and the response carries &#x60;authUrl&#x60; only (no &#x60;state&#x60;). That page opens Meta&#39;s Embedded Signup popup itself, so it connects exactly the WhatsApp Business Account and number the user picked in the popup.  **When to use it**: your users&#39; Facebook logins manage several WhatsApp accounts. On the default redirect flow Meta only returns an authorization code, so when that login can see more than one number the user lands on Zernio&#39;s number picker and has to choose again.  **Flow**: nothing to embed and no domain setup. Send the user to &#x60;authUrl&#x60;; they come back to &#x60;redirect_url&#x60; with the same params as the redirect flow.  - Success: &#x60;connected&#x3D;whatsapp&#x60;, &#x60;profileId&#x60;, &#x60;accountId&#x60;, &#x60;username&#x60; (plus &#x60;connect_token&#x60; for API-key callers). - Failure: &#x60;error&#x60; and &#x60;platform&#x3D;whatsapp&#x60;, with the same values and extras as the redirect flow (see below), plus two of its own.  Redirect-flow failures: &#x60;one_whatsapp_per_profile&#x60;, &#x60;whatsapp_number_already_connected&#x60;, &#x60;whatsapp_number_pinned_to_profile&#x60; and &#x60;whatsapp_coexistence_not_registered&#x60; with &#x60;is_user_fixable&#x3D;true&#x60;; &#x60;payment_required&#x60; with &#x60;reason&#x60; and &#x60;dashboard_url&#x60;; &#x60;whatsapp_error&#x60; with &#x60;error_message&#x60; when Meta reported one.  Hosted-only failures:  - &#x60;connection_cancelled&#x60;: the popup was closed before finishing (&#x60;error_message&#x60; carries Meta&#39;s last reported step or error when there is one). - &#x60;session_expired&#x60;: the user took longer than the 60 minute window the hosted page is valid for. Restart the flow with a new call.  **Same as the redirect flow**: &#x60;onboarding&#x60; is carried through, and a pre-verified Zernio-provisioned number is attached.  When a previously disconnected account for this profile can simply be re-enabled, this endpoint re-enables it and returns the account directly instead of a URL. &#x60;headless&#x60; has no effect, because there is no selection step left to hand you.  **The page** shows the same guidance as the Zernio dashboard: a pre-verified Zernio-provisioned number is called out by name (\&quot;choose it in Meta&#39;s list, no code will be asked\&quot;).  Coexistence and standard signups get their explainer video, and a step-by-step checklist stays visible while Meta&#39;s popup is open. Skin it with &#x60;brandName&#x60;, &#x60;primaryColor&#x60; and &#x60;language&#x60; below. 
    # @option opts [String] :brand_name Your product name, for the two branded pages. Trimmed; 1 to 60 characters.  - With &#x60;signup&#x3D;hosted&#x60; (WhatsApp): replaces Zernio in the page title (\&quot;Connect your WhatsApp number to &lt;brandName&gt;\&quot;). - With &#x60;welcome&#x3D;true&#x60;: fills the heading (\&quot;&lt;brandName&gt; wants to connect to your &lt;platform&gt;\&quot;). Without it the screen shows Zernio and the Zernio mark.  Both pages keep a Zernio mark: they are co-branded, not white-label. Rejected with 400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60; without &#x60;signup&#x3D;hosted&#x60; or &#x60;welcome&#x3D;true&#x60;. Sealed into the page link at issue time, so editing the URL cannot change it. 
    # @option opts [String] :primary_color Hex colour (&#x60;#RRGGBB&#x60;) for the primary button on the hosted WhatsApp signup page (&#x60;signup&#x3D;hosted&#x60;) or the welcome screen (&#x60;welcome&#x3D;true&#x60;). Validated server-side; anything else is a 400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60;. Rejected without one of the two.
    # @option opts [Boolean] :welcome Any platform. When &#x60;true&#x60;, &#x60;authUrl&#x60; points to a Zernio-hosted welcome screen showing your brand next to the platform (\&quot;&lt;brandName&gt; wants to connect to your &lt;platform&gt;\&quot;). Its button reads Connecting for about a second, then sends the user to the platform&#39;s authorization screen with no click.  The rest of the flow is unchanged.  - &#x60;brandName&#x60;, &#x60;logoUrl&#x60;, &#x60;primaryColor&#x60; and &#x60;welcomeTheme&#x60; are optional and default to Zernio&#39;s own name, mark and look. - The link is valid for 30 minutes; after that the page asks the user to start again. - The brand also carries to the account and channel pickers Zernio shows after authorization. - With no &#x60;redirect_url&#x60;, the flow ends on a branded Zernio-hosted page saying whether the account connected, instead of the Zernio dashboard. - Cannot be combined with &#x60;headless&#x3D;true&#x60; or &#x60;signup&#x3D;hosted&#x60; (400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60;). - The platform&#39;s authorization screen still names the Zernio app.  Recommended. When left out, the screen is shown if the workspace saved it as on by default (&#x60;PUT /v1/connect/welcome-screen&#x60;), except with &#x60;headless&#x3D;true&#x60; or &#x60;signup&#x3D;hosted&#x60;. Pass &#x60;false&#x60; to skip it.  Branding you leave out of the call comes from those saved settings, and a &#x60;welcomeTheme&#x60; you send is merged key by key over the saved theme. 
    # @option opts [String] :welcome_theme Welcome screen only (&#x60;welcome&#x3D;true&#x60;). A URL-encoded JSON object that restyles and rewords the screen. All keys are optional.  - **Copy**: &#x60;heading&#x60; (up to 120 characters); &#x60;trustLine&#x60;, &#x60;consentLine&#x60; and &#x60;statusLine&#x60; (up to 200 each, &#x60;statusLine&#x60; being the line above the button); &#x60;buttonLabel&#x60; (up to 30, the label of the link the button becomes if the redirect stalls). - **Closing page** (shown when there is no &#x60;redirect_url&#x60;): &#x60;successHeading&#x60; and &#x60;errorHeading&#x60; (up to 120), &#x60;successBody&#x60; and &#x60;errorBody&#x60; (up to 200). All copy may contain the placeholders &#x60;{brand}&#x60; and &#x60;{platform}&#x60;. - **Colors**: &#x60;primaryColor&#x60; (the button), &#x60;accentColor&#x60; (the header gradient, built as a scale of that colour, and the icons), &#x60;pageColor&#x60;, &#x60;cardColor&#x60; and &#x60;textColor&#x60;, all as &#x60;#RRGGBB&#x60;. - **Style**: &#x60;cornerRadius&#x60; as an integer from 0 to 24 (pixels); &#x60;font&#x60; as &#x60;sans&#x60;, &#x60;serif&#x60; or &#x60;mono&#x60;; &#x60;bannerStyle&#x60; as &#x60;halftone&#x60; (default), &#x60;solid&#x60; (a flat tint of &#x60;accentColor&#x60;) or &#x60;plain&#x60; (no banner fill). - **Icons**: &#x60;trustLineIcon&#x60; (default &#x60;shield&#x60;) and &#x60;consentLineIcon&#x60; (default &#x60;link&#x60;), each one of &#x60;shield&#x60;, &#x60;lock&#x60;, &#x60;link&#x60;, &#x60;check&#x60;, &#x60;user&#x60;, &#x60;sparkles&#x60; or &#x60;none&#x60;. - **Visibility**: &#x60;hide&#x60;, an array of any of &#x60;heading&#x60;, &#x60;trustLine&#x60;, &#x60;consentLine&#x60;, &#x60;statusLine&#x60;, &#x60;successBody&#x60; and &#x60;errorBody&#x60;, removes those lines from the screens. - **Links**: &#x60;termsUrl&#x60; and &#x60;privacyUrl&#x60; (https, up to 2048 characters) add small Terms and Privacy links at the bottom of every hosted screen.  A &#x60;primaryColor&#x60; here wins over the &#x60;primaryColor&#x60; parameter. Unknown keys, invalid JSON or an invalid value are a 400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60;. Rejected when the welcome screen is not shown.  Example: &#x60;{\&quot;heading\&quot;:\&quot;Link your {platform} to {brand}\&quot;,\&quot;cardColor\&quot;:\&quot;#FFF7ED\&quot;,\&quot;cornerRadius\&quot;:12}&#x60;. 
    # @option opts [String] :logo_url Welcome screen only (&#x60;welcome&#x3D;true&#x60;): https URL of your logo, shown in a square tile, so use a square image. Without it the tile shows the first letter of &#x60;brandName&#x60;, or the Zernio mark when there is no &#x60;brandName&#x60; either. Rejected with 400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60; when the welcome screen is not shown.
    # @option opts [String] :language Hosted signup page only (&#x60;signup&#x3D;hosted&#x60;, WhatsApp): language of the page and its follow-along guide. Explainer videos stay in English. Default &#x60;en&#x60;. Rejected without &#x60;signup&#x3D;hosted&#x60;.
    # @option opts [Boolean] :handoff Let the user finish on their phone. When &#x60;true&#x60;, the response also carries &#x60;handoff&#x60;. Show &#x60;handoff.url&#x60; as a QR code in your app (any QR library); the user scans it and the welcome screen opens on the phone, already carrying this connect.  They log in to the platform there without signing in to anything else. The phone ends on a Zernio result screen telling them to go back to their computer.  - Learn the outcome by polling &#x60;GET /v1/connect/handoffs/{handoffId}&#x60; (every 2 to 5 seconds is fine) or from the &#x60;account.connected&#x60; webhook. - Shows the welcome screen with your branding parameters or saved settings. - Cannot be combined with &#x60;welcome&#x3D;false&#x60;, &#x60;headless&#x3D;true&#x60;, &#x60;signup&#x60;, &#x60;redirect&#x3D;true&#x60; or &#x60;redirect_url&#x60; (400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60;). - &#x60;handoff.url&#x60; works for 30 minutes. - When the account is re-enabled straight away, the response carries &#x60;account&#x60; instead, as without &#x60;handoff&#x60;.  (default to false)
    # @return [GetConnectUrl200Response]
    def get_connect_url(platform, profile_id, opts = {})
      data, _status_code, _headers = get_connect_url_with_http_info(platform, profile_id, opts)
      data
    end

    # Get OAuth connect URL
    # Initiate an OAuth connection flow. Returns an authUrl to redirect the user to.  ### Modes  - Standard flow: Zernio hosts the selection UI, then redirects to your redirect_url. - Headless mode (headless&#x3D;true): user is redirected to your redirect_url with OAuth data for custom UI. Use the platform-specific selection endpoints to complete.  ### Several accounts per platform  A profile can hold several accounts of the same platform. Connecting a different account adds it as a new account, and reconnecting the SAME account keeps it and all of its history.  Ads connections stay one per profile.  On a legacy plan limited to N profiles, a new account is refused with 403 &#x60;platform_account_limit&#x60; once N accounts of its platform are connected.  ### TikTok  Every connection now goes through the TikTok for Business app.  An authorization that leaves out a permission the connected account needs changes nothing at all and comes back as &#x60;missing_tiktok_permissions&#x60;. Connect again and accept every permission on TikTok&#39;s screen. 
    # @param platform [String] Social media platform to connect. &#x60;snapchat&#x60; is a closed beta with no public release date: it returns 403 &#x60;PLATFORM_BETA_RESTRICTED&#x60; until the account is approved.
    # @param profile_id [String] Your Zernio profile ID (get from /v1/profiles). For WhatsApp, a Zernio-provisioned number can only be connected on the profile it was provisioned to; connecting from any other profile is rejected with a 409.
    # @param [Hash] opts the optional parameters
    # @option opts [String] :reconnect_account_id Refresh this existing account: a Zernio account id of the same platform on this profile (otherwise 400).  The OAuth callback and the selection endpoints (select-page, select-organization, select-board, select-location, Instagram and Snapchat selection) refuse with &#x60;reconnect_account_mismatch&#x60; a login that would write to a different account of the platform on this profile instead of this one.  In headless mode the marker travels in the redirect_url we hand you, so pass that URL back unchanged to the selection endpoint. On X it counts toward the OAuth state limit described under redirect_url. 
    # @option opts [String] :oauth_app_id Connect through one of your own OAuth apps (see /v1/connect/oauth-apps), so the consent screen shows your app and the platform&#39;s limits are your app&#39;s. Without it the connect runs on Zernio&#39;s app, whatever apps the workspace has saved.  - Only platforms listed in &#x60;platforms&#x60; of GET /v1/connect/oauth-apps accept an app. Any other returns 400, and so do ads connects (&#x60;adsConnect&#x3D;true&#x60; in the redirect URL). - Connects that end on a destination picker also return 400, except Facebook Pages, Google Business locations, Pinterest boards and Snapchat public profiles (Instagram through Facebook Login, for example). - A LinkedIn connect through an app saves the member&#39;s own profile: organization pages, and mention lookups, stay on Zernio&#39;s app. - The connect requests the app&#39;s &#x60;scopeAreas&#x60;. &#x60;scopes&#x60; may narrow them but not add an area the app does not enable (400). - If the user does not grant every requested area, the account still connects and the redirect carries &#x60;missing_permissions&#x3D;&lt;areas&gt;&#x60; (the headless POST returns &#x60;missingPermissions&#x60;). - If the platform refuses a permission your app is not approved for, the redirect carries &#x60;error&#x3D;oauth_app_scope_not_allowed&#x60;.  The account remembers the app, and token refresh, publishing and inbox run on it. Reconnecting through another app, or without one, moves the account to that app. 
    # @option opts [String] :expected_platform_user_id Only connect if the login lands on this platform account. Any other account ends the flow with &#x60;error&#x3D;account_mismatch&#x60; (a 409 &#x60;account_mismatch&#x60; on POST /v1/connect/instagram/select-account) and nothing is written.  Compared with every id the platform reports for the authorized account:  - Any platform: the &#x60;platformUserId&#x60; of a Zernio account on this platform. - Instagram: either the app-scoped id or the professional account id (&#x60;metadata.instagramScopedId&#x60;, the &#x60;17841...&#x60; id that Facebook Login accounts hold as platformUserId). - TikTok: open_ids are app-scoped, so an id from your own TikTok app never matches. Use expectedUsername there.  Honoured by the OAuth callback (every platform that connects without a selection step, Instagram Login included) and by the Instagram selection step. On the other selection endpoints you choose the destination yourself.  In headless mode the marker travels in the redirect_url we hand you, so pass that URL back unchanged. On X it counts toward the OAuth state limit described under redirect_url. 
    # @option opts [String] :expected_username Only connect if the authorized account&#39;s handle is this one (case-insensitive, a leading @ is ignored). Otherwise the flow ends with &#x60;error&#x3D;account_mismatch&#x60; and &#x60;error_message&#x60; naming the handle that was authorized, and nothing is written.  Same coverage and transport as expectedPlatformUserId; when both are sent, both must match. Use this on a first connection, where you hold the handle the user typed but no Zernio id yet. 
    # @option opts [Boolean] :force_reauth Instagram Login only (the default loginMethod); ignored elsewhere. Makes Instagram show its login page and ask for the credentials of the account to connect, even when another Instagram account is logged in on the device or app. Also hides the Facebook login option on that page.  Use it when the person connecting manages several Instagram accounts on one phone: otherwise Instagram logs in, and converts to a professional account, whichever account is active, before any consent screen. Pair it with expectedUsername to also refuse a wrong account at the end.  (default to false)
    # @option opts [String] :redirect_url Your custom redirect URL after the connection completes. It MUST be an absolute http(s) URL or a custom app scheme for mobile deeplinks (e.g. myapp://callback). A relative path is rejected with 400 &#x60;INVALID_REDIRECT_URL&#x60;.  **Exit notice:** when &#x60;redirect_url&#x60; is an http(s) URL on another site (anything but zernio.com), every redirect of the flow lands first on &#x60;https://zernio.com/connect/continue?to&#x3D;&lt;your URL&gt;&#x60;, a Zernio page that names your site and continues to it with one click. All params below reach your URL unchanged.  A custom app scheme (myapp://...) never goes through the notice. In headless mode the redirects we hand you (and the &#x60;redirect_url&#x60; returned by the selection endpoints) are notice URLs: pass them back or navigate to them as they are.  **X (twitter) length limit:** X caps the OAuth &#x60;state&#x60; at 500 characters and the redirect travels inside it (wrapped in the notice URL for an http(s) URL on another site). The URL-encoded form must be at most 258 characters for API callers, 310 for dashboard sessions.  In headless mode the appended &#x60;headless&#x3D;true&#x60; counts toward that limit. A plain https URL on another site leaves about 165 to 190 characters of your own URL, depending on encoding. A longer one is rejected with 400 &#x60;INVALID_REDIRECT_URL&#x60;, and the error says by how much.  **Success params** are appended with the URL API, so an existing query string is preserved:  - Standard mode: connected&#x3D;{platform}&amp;profileId&#x3D;X&amp;accountId&#x3D;Y&amp;username&#x3D;Z. - Headless mode: OAuth data params for platforms requiring selection (e.g. LinkedIn orgs, Facebook pages). If no selection is needed, the account is created directly and the redirect includes accountId.  **Failure params:** the browser goes to the same redirect_url with &#x60;error&#x60; and &#x60;platform&#x60; appended (always present). &#x60;error_message&#x60;, &#x60;is_user_fixable&#x60;, &#x60;reason&#x60;, &#x60;dashboard_url&#x60;, &#x60;missing_scopes&#x60;, &#x60;error_reason&#x60; and the &#x60;platform_error*&#x60; params are conditional: treat them as optional.  Your own query params are kept on every redirect, but ours overwrite one of yours with the same name. On an error redirect we remove the internal &#x60;headless&#x60;, &#x60;adsConnect&#x60;, &#x60;adsScope&#x60;, &#x60;reconnectAccountId&#x60;, &#x60;expectedPlatformUserId&#x60; and &#x60;expectedUsername&#x60; markers added during the flow.  **Correlation** params appear on every redirect from an OAuth callback (success and failure) and on the &#x60;redirect_url&#x60; returned by the selection endpoints such as POST /v1/connect/facebook/select-page:  - &#x60;request_id&#x60;: the id we log that request under. Quote it when reporting a problem. - &#x60;stage&#x60;: where the flow ended. &#x60;authorize&#x60; &#x3D; the platform&#39;s consent dialog returned an error or denial instead of a code. &#x60;callback&#x60; &#x3D; we processed the returned code (success, a selection step, or a failure). - &#x60;stage&#x60; &#x3D; &#x60;select_page&#x60;: the destination-selection endpoint (page, account, organization, board, location, profile or phone number) completed it.  **Error details:**  - &#x60;oauth_denied&#x60;: carries &#x60;error_message&#x60; and, when the platform sent them, its own &#x60;platform_error&#x60; (e.g. &#x60;access_denied&#x60;), &#x60;platform_error_reason&#x60; (e.g. &#x60;user_denied&#x60;) and &#x60;platform_error_description&#x60; (truncated to 500 characters). &#x60;is_user_fixable&#x3D;true&#x60; when the platform reported that the user cancelled or declined. - &#x60;no_facebook_pages&#x60;: comes with &#x60;is_user_fixable&#x3D;true&#x60;, an &#x60;error_message&#x60; telling the user to click \&quot;Edit previous settings\&quot; in Meta&#39;s dialog and tick the Page (or create one), and &#x60;error_reason&#x60; when Meta&#39;s token debug answered (values below). - &#x60;code_already_redeemed&#x60;: the same authorization code arrived more than once and an earlier request already processed it (the code is never sent to the platform twice). Not a failure: check GET /v1/accounts or wait for the &#x60;account.connected&#x60; webhook. - &#x60;missing_google_permissions&#x60; (YouTube, Google Business and Google Ads): the user unchecked permissions on Google&#39;s consent screen. Always with &#x60;is_user_fixable&#x3D;true&#x60;. When Google reported granted scopes, &#x60;missing_scopes&#x60; lists the requested scopes not granted (comma-separated). Ask the user to connect again keeping every permission checked. - &#x60;no_youtube_channel&#x60;: Google authorized the account but it has no YouTube channel we can connect. Always with &#x60;is_user_fixable&#x3D;true&#x60; and an &#x60;error_message&#x60;.  Usual causes of &#x60;no_youtube_channel&#x60;: the user picked their personal Google identity instead of the Brand Account in Google&#39;s account chooser, they only have YouTube Studio access (not Brand Account owner or manager), or the account has no channel yet.  &#x60;error_reason&#x60; values for &#x60;no_facebook_pages&#x60;:  - &#x60;pages_permission_declined&#x60;: the user declined the pages_show_list permission. - &#x60;no_pages_granted&#x60;: the permission was granted with no Page ticked. Meta reports a user who manages no Page the same way, so this covers both. - &#x60;granted_pages_not_listed&#x60;: Pages were ticked but Meta listed none the user can manage, and a direct read of each ticked Page returned no access token.  **Headless &#x60;userProfile&#x60;:** on headless Facebook success (&#x60;step&#x3D;select_page&#x60;) and headless Instagram &#x60;facebook_login&#x60; success (&#x60;step&#x3D;select_account&#x60;), &#x60;userProfile&#x60; is JSON percent-encoded once before being set as a query param, so it is encoded twice on the wire.  After your framework decodes the query string once, run one more decodeURIComponent (or equivalent), then JSON.parse it. &#x60;tempToken&#x60; and &#x60;connect_token&#x60; are plain values.  **Error values.** This list is NOT exhaustive and new values may be added at any time: treat an unrecognized value as a generic failure rather than matching exhaustively. Existing values are not renamed or removed without notice.  - OAuth and callback: &#x60;oauth_denied&#x60;, &#x60;invalid_callback&#x60;, &#x60;invalid_state&#x60;, &#x60;unsupported_platform&#x60;, &#x60;connection_failed&#x60;, &#x60;internal_error&#x60;, &#x60;token_exchange_failed&#x60;, &#x60;byok_config_error&#x60;, &#x60;personal_account_not_supported&#x60;, &#x60;missing_google_permissions&#x60;, &#x60;missing_tiktok_permissions&#x60;, &#x60;platform_requires_destination&#x60;, &#x60;reconnect_account_mismatch&#x60;, &#x60;account_mismatch&#x60;, &#x60;instagram_login_method_mismatch&#x60;, &#x60;invalid_request&#x60;, &#x60;code_already_redeemed&#x60;. - Access and limits: &#x60;profile_not_found&#x60;, &#x60;invalid_profile_id&#x60;, &#x60;access_denied&#x60;, &#x60;account_limit_exceeded&#x60;, &#x60;profile_limit_exceeded&#x60;, &#x60;payment_required&#x60;. - Destination selection: &#x60;no_facebook_pages&#x60;, &#x60;facebook_pages_error&#x60;, &#x60;no_google_locations&#x60;, &#x60;google_locations_error&#x60;, &#x60;google_permission_denied&#x60;, &#x60;no_snapchat_public_profiles&#x60;, &#x60;snapchat_profiles_error&#x60;, &#x60;no_youtube_channel&#x60;, &#x60;discord_no_guild&#x60;, &#x60;slack_no_team&#x60;. - WhatsApp: &#x60;whatsapp_error&#x60;, &#x60;one_whatsapp_per_profile&#x60;, &#x60;whatsapp_number_already_connected&#x60;, &#x60;whatsapp_number_pinned_to_profile&#x60;, &#x60;whatsapp_coexistence_not_registered&#x60;, &#x60;connection_cancelled&#x60;. - Google Ads (platform&#x3D;googleads): &#x60;google_ads_auth_failed&#x60;, &#x60;google_ads_invalid_state&#x60;, &#x60;google_ads_config_error&#x60;, &#x60;google_ads_token_failed&#x60;, &#x60;google_ads_quota_exhausted&#x60;, &#x60;google_ads_callback_error&#x60;. - TikTok Ads (platform&#x3D;tiktokads): &#x60;tiktok_ads_auth_failed&#x60;, &#x60;tiktok_ads_invalid_state&#x60;, &#x60;tiktok_ads_access_denied&#x60;, &#x60;tiktok_ads_config_error&#x60;, &#x60;tiktok_ads_token_failed&#x60;, &#x60;tiktok_ads_account_not_found&#x60;, &#x60;tiktok_ads_callback_error&#x60;. - X Ads (platform&#x3D;xads): &#x60;x_ads_denied&#x60;, &#x60;x_ads_auth_failed&#x60;, &#x60;x_ads_config_error&#x60;, &#x60;x_ads_account_not_found&#x60;, &#x60;x_ads_state_error&#x60;, &#x60;x_ads_token_failed&#x60;, &#x60;x_ads_token_missing&#x60;, &#x60;x_ads_callback_error&#x60;. - Reddit Ads (platform&#x3D;redditads): &#x60;reddit_ads_auth_failed&#x60;, &#x60;reddit_ads_invalid_state&#x60;, &#x60;reddit_ads_access_denied&#x60;, &#x60;reddit_ads_scope_not_granted&#x60;, &#x60;reddit_ads_no_ad_accounts&#x60;, &#x60;reddit_ads_callback_error&#x60;. - Shopify (platform&#x3D;shopify): &#x60;shopify_auth_failed&#x60;, &#x60;shopify_config_error&#x60;, &#x60;shopify_invalid_state&#x60;, &#x60;shopify_invalid_hmac&#x60;, &#x60;shopify_invalid_shop&#x60;, &#x60;shopify_missing_scopes&#x60;, &#x60;shopify_callback_error&#x60;.  Notes:  1. On this endpoint every upstream OAuth error collapses into &#x60;oauth_denied&#x60;, with the provider&#39;s values in the &#x60;platform_error*&#x60; params. The dedicated ads flows differ: they use their own denial slugs, and &#x60;google_ads_auth_failed&#x60; and &#x60;tiktok_ads_auth_failed&#x60; may carry the provider&#39;s raw error string in &#x60;error_message&#x60;. 2. On the tiktok and twitter ads flows &#x60;platform&#x60; carries the ads platform id (&#x60;tiktokads&#x60;, &#x60;xads&#x60;), not the value in the request path. The googleads, redditads and shopify flows report &#x60;googleads&#x60;, &#x60;redditads&#x60; and &#x60;shopify&#x60;. 3. &#x60;missing_tiktok_permissions&#x60;: the TikTok authorization left out a permission the already-connected account needs, so nothing changed and it keeps working as before. User-fixable: connect again and accept every permission on TikTok&#39;s screen. 4. &#x60;instagram_login_method_mismatch&#x60;: an Instagram Login authorization landed on a profile whose Instagram account is connected through Facebook Login, so nothing changed. To refresh it, connect again with &#x60;loginMethod&#x3D;facebook_login&#x60;. To move it to Instagram Login, disconnect it first. 
    # @option opts [String] :scopes Comma-separated permission areas to request instead of the platform&#39;s full permission set.  **Values:** &#x60;posting&#x60;, &#x60;analytics&#x60;, &#x60;comments&#x60;, &#x60;messaging&#x60;, &#x60;ads&#x60;; on google and microsoft, &#x60;email&#x60;, &#x60;calendar&#x60;, &#x60;files&#x60;, &#x60;contacts&#x60;.  **Default:** omit it (what the dashboard does) to request everything the platform supports. Google and microsoft REQUIRE it (400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60; when absent) because their consent screens are reviewed per area.  When present, the consent dialog asks only for the scopes behind those areas, plus the scopes every connection needs (identity, token refresh, listing the pages, organizations or channels the user picks from).  - Scopes never asked for are absent from the account&#39;s &#x60;permissions&#x60;, and the health endpoints report them as not granted. A &#x60;posting&#x60;-only account cannot read analytics or the inbox until reconnected with more areas. - First comments need &#x60;comments&#x60;: a &#x60;posting&#x60;-only account publishes the post and skips the first comment. - Scopes in none of the areas (X likes, bookmarks and follows, Pinterest ads-only extras) are requested only when the parameter is omitted.  **Supported on** facebook, instagram (both login methods), linkedin, twitter, tiktok, youtube, threads, reddit, pinterest, googlebusiness and slack (via &#x60;GET /v1/connect/slack&#x60;).  **Rejected** with 400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60; (&#x60;param: scopes&#x60;) on bluesky, telegram, discord, snapchat and whatsapp (their dialog cannot be reduced), and for an empty list or an unknown area.  What each area asks for, per platform (Google scopes shortened to their last path segment):  | Platform | &#x60;posting&#x60; | &#x60;analytics&#x60; | &#x60;comments&#x60; | &#x60;messaging&#x60; | &#x60;ads&#x60; | Always requested | |---|---|---|---|---|---|---| | facebook | &#x60;pages_manage_posts&#x60; | &#x60;read_insights&#x60;, &#x60;pages_read_user_content&#x60; | &#x60;pages_manage_engagement&#x60;, &#x60;pages_read_user_content&#x60; | &#x60;pages_messaging&#x60; | &#x60;ads_management&#x60;, &#x60;ads_read&#x60;, &#x60;leads_retrieval&#x60;, &#x60;pages_manage_ads&#x60;, &#x60;instagram_basic&#x60;, &#x60;business_management&#x60; | &#x60;pages_show_list&#x60;, &#x60;pages_read_engagement&#x60;, &#x60;pages_manage_metadata&#x60; | | instagram (Instagram Login) | &#x60;instagram_business_content_publish&#x60; | &#x60;instagram_business_manage_insights&#x60; | &#x60;instagram_business_manage_comments&#x60; | &#x60;instagram_business_manage_messages&#x60; | none | &#x60;instagram_business_basic&#x60; | | instagram (&#x60;loginMethod&#x3D;facebook_login&#x60;) | &#x60;instagram_content_publish&#x60; | &#x60;instagram_manage_insights&#x60; | &#x60;instagram_manage_comments&#x60; | &#x60;instagram_manage_messages&#x60; | &#x60;ads_management&#x60;, &#x60;ads_read&#x60;, &#x60;leads_retrieval&#x60;, &#x60;pages_manage_ads&#x60; | &#x60;instagram_basic&#x60;, &#x60;pages_show_list&#x60;, &#x60;pages_read_engagement&#x60;, &#x60;business_management&#x60;, &#x60;pages_messaging&#x60;, &#x60;pages_manage_metadata&#x60; | | linkedin | &#x60;w_member_social&#x60;, &#x60;w_organization_social&#x60;, &#x60;r_organization_social&#x60;, &#x60;r_organization_followers&#x60; | &#x60;r_member_postAnalytics&#x60;, &#x60;r_member_profileAnalytics&#x60;, &#x60;rw_organization_admin&#x60;, &#x60;r_organization_social&#x60;, &#x60;r_organization_followers&#x60; | &#x60;w_member_social&#x60;, &#x60;w_member_social_feed&#x60;, &#x60;w_organization_social&#x60;, &#x60;w_organization_social_feed&#x60;, &#x60;r_organization_social&#x60;, &#x60;r_organization_social_feed&#x60; | none | &#x60;r_ads&#x60;, &#x60;rw_ads&#x60;, &#x60;r_ads_reporting&#x60;, &#x60;r_marketing_leadgen_automation&#x60;, &#x60;rw_conversions&#x60; | &#x60;openid&#x60;, &#x60;profile&#x60;, &#x60;email&#x60;, &#x60;r_basicprofile&#x60;, &#x60;rw_organization_admin&#x60; | | twitter | &#x60;tweet.write&#x60;, &#x60;media.write&#x60; | (in the always-requested set) | &#x60;tweet.write&#x60;, &#x60;like.write&#x60;, &#x60;tweet.moderate.write&#x60; | &#x60;dm.read&#x60;, &#x60;dm.write&#x60;, &#x60;media.write&#x60; | none | &#x60;tweet.read&#x60;, &#x60;users.read&#x60;, &#x60;offline.access&#x60; | | tiktok | &#x60;video.publish&#x60; | &#x60;user.info.stats&#x60;, &#x60;user.insights&#x60;, &#x60;video.list&#x60;, &#x60;video.insights&#x60; | &#x60;comment.list&#x60;, &#x60;comment.list.manage&#x60;, &#x60;video.list&#x60; | &#x60;message.list.read&#x60;, &#x60;message.list.send&#x60;, &#x60;message.list.manage&#x60; | none | &#x60;user.info.basic&#x60;, &#x60;user.info.username&#x60;, &#x60;user.info.profile&#x60;, &#x60;user.account.type&#x60;, &#x60;video.publish&#x60;, &#x60;video.upload&#x60;, &#x60;video.list&#x60; | | youtube | &#x60;youtube.upload&#x60; | &#x60;yt-analytics.readonly&#x60; | &#x60;youtube.force-ssl&#x60; | none | none | &#x60;youtube&#x60; | | threads | &#x60;threads_content_publish&#x60;, &#x60;threads_manage_replies&#x60;, &#x60;threads_delete&#x60; | &#x60;threads_manage_insights&#x60; | &#x60;threads_content_publish&#x60;, &#x60;threads_read_replies&#x60;, &#x60;threads_manage_replies&#x60;, &#x60;threads_delete&#x60; | none | none | &#x60;threads_basic&#x60; | | reddit | &#x60;submit&#x60;, &#x60;read&#x60;, &#x60;mysubreddits&#x60;, &#x60;flair&#x60;, &#x60;history&#x60;, &#x60;edit&#x60; | &#x60;read&#x60;, &#x60;history&#x60; | &#x60;read&#x60;, &#x60;history&#x60;, &#x60;edit&#x60;, &#x60;vote&#x60; | &#x60;privatemessages&#x60; | none | &#x60;identity&#x60; | | pinterest | &#x60;boards:write&#x60;, &#x60;pins:read&#x60;, &#x60;pins:write&#x60; | &#x60;pins:read&#x60;, &#x60;user_accounts:read&#x60; | none | none | &#x60;ads:read&#x60;, &#x60;ads:write&#x60;, &#x60;boards:write&#x60;, &#x60;pins:read&#x60;, &#x60;pins:write&#x60; | &#x60;boards:read&#x60;, &#x60;user_accounts:read&#x60; | | googlebusiness | &#x60;business.manage&#x60; | &#x60;business.manage&#x60; | &#x60;business.manage&#x60; | none | none | &#x60;business.manage&#x60;, &#x60;userinfo.profile&#x60;, &#x60;userinfo.email&#x60; | | slack | &#x60;chat:write&#x60;, &#x60;chat:write.public&#x60;, &#x60;chat:write.customize&#x60;, &#x60;files:write&#x60;, &#x60;files:read&#x60; | none | none | &#x60;chat:write&#x60;, &#x60;chat:write.customize&#x60;, &#x60;files:write&#x60;, &#x60;files:read&#x60;, &#x60;channels:history&#x60;, &#x60;groups:history&#x60;, &#x60;im:history&#x60;, &#x60;mpim:history&#x60;, &#x60;im:read&#x60;, &#x60;im:write&#x60;, &#x60;mpim:read&#x60;, &#x60;users:read&#x60;, &#x60;reactions:read&#x60;, &#x60;reactions:write&#x60; | none | &#x60;channels:join&#x60;, &#x60;channels:read&#x60;, &#x60;groups:read&#x60;, &#x60;team:read&#x60; |  Google and Microsoft accounts use the mailbox areas instead (&#x60;scopes&#x60; is required there):  | Platform | &#x60;email&#x60; | &#x60;calendar&#x60; | &#x60;files&#x60; | &#x60;contacts&#x60; | Always requested | |---|---|---|---|---|---| | google | &#x60;gmail.modify&#x60; | &#x60;calendar&#x60; | &#x60;drive.file&#x60; (only files Zernio created or the user picked, see the Files tag) | &#x60;contacts.readonly&#x60; | &#x60;openid&#x60;, &#x60;userinfo.email&#x60;, &#x60;userinfo.profile&#x60; | | microsoft | &#x60;Mail.ReadWrite&#x60;, &#x60;Mail.Send&#x60; | &#x60;Calendars.ReadWrite&#x60; | &#x60;Files.ReadWrite&#x60; | &#x60;Contacts.Read&#x60; | &#x60;openid&#x60;, &#x60;profile&#x60;, &#x60;email&#x60;, &#x60;offline_access&#x60;, &#x60;User.Read&#x60; |  Areas accumulate: reconnecting with more areas widens the grant, and &#x60;GET /v1/accounts/{accountId}/health&#x60; reports the result. 
    # @option opts [String] :login_hint google and microsoft only: pre-fills the account picker with this address so the user lands on the right mailbox.
    # @option opts [Boolean] :headless When true, the user is redirected to your redirect_url with raw OAuth data (code, state) instead of Zernio&#39;s default account selection UI. Use this to build a custom connect experience. (default to false)
    # @option opts [String] :login_method Instagram only: which of the two Instagram connection methods to use. Ignored for every other platform.  - &#x60;instagram_login&#x60; (default when omitted): the Instagram Login dialog. The user authorizes their Instagram professional account directly, no Facebook Page required. Exception: if omitted and &#x60;reconnectAccountId&#x60; names an account connected with &#x60;facebook_login&#x60;, the reconnect keeps that method. - &#x60;facebook_login&#x60;: the Facebook Login dialog (\&quot;Instagram API with Facebook Login\&quot;). The user authorizes a Facebook Page with a linked Instagram professional account, and every API call for that account runs through the Page. Use it when the customer manages Instagram through a Page and expects the Facebook consent screen.  With &#x60;facebook_login&#x60; the user picks a Page, so the callback continues at the account-selection step, &#x60;/v1/connect/instagram/select-account&#x60;. The default &#x60;instagram_login&#x60; has no selection step and connects directly.  &#x60;facebook_login&#x60; supports &#x60;headless&#x3D;true&#x60; like the other selection platforms. The callback redirects to your &#x60;redirect_url&#x60; with &#x60;profileId&#x60;, &#x60;tempToken&#x60;, &#x60;platform&#x3D;instagram&#x60;, &#x60;step&#x3D;select_account&#x60;, &#x60;userProfile&#x60; and &#x60;connect_token&#x60;.  &#x60;userProfile&#x60; is the Facebook user&#39;s profile, same shape and encoding as the Facebook &#x60;step&#x3D;select_page&#x60; redirect. Pass &#x60;profileId&#x60;, &#x60;tempToken&#x60; and &#x60;connect_token&#x60; into the select-account endpoints to finish.  (default to 'instagram_login')
    # @option opts [String] :onboarding WhatsApp only. Ignored for every other platform. Controls which screen Meta&#39;s Embedded Signup popup shows.  If omitted, the connection defaults to coexistence (same as &#x60;business_app&#x60; below), preserving existing behavior for numbers already on the WhatsApp Business app.  &#x60;api&#x60;: standard Embedded Signup, showing Meta&#39;s WABA/number picker. Use this to connect a phone number already on Cloud API elsewhere.  &#x60;business_app&#x60;: coexistence, i.e. &#39;Connect existing WhatsApp Business app&#39; (a number shared between Cloud API and the consumer WhatsApp Business app). 
    # @option opts [String] :signup WhatsApp only. Rejected with 400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60; on any other platform.  &#x60;hosted&#x60;: &#x60;authUrl&#x60; points at a Zernio-hosted page on zernio.com instead of Meta&#39;s OAuth dialog, and the response carries &#x60;authUrl&#x60; only (no &#x60;state&#x60;). That page opens Meta&#39;s Embedded Signup popup itself, so it connects exactly the WhatsApp Business Account and number the user picked in the popup.  **When to use it**: your users&#39; Facebook logins manage several WhatsApp accounts. On the default redirect flow Meta only returns an authorization code, so when that login can see more than one number the user lands on Zernio&#39;s number picker and has to choose again.  **Flow**: nothing to embed and no domain setup. Send the user to &#x60;authUrl&#x60;; they come back to &#x60;redirect_url&#x60; with the same params as the redirect flow.  - Success: &#x60;connected&#x3D;whatsapp&#x60;, &#x60;profileId&#x60;, &#x60;accountId&#x60;, &#x60;username&#x60; (plus &#x60;connect_token&#x60; for API-key callers). - Failure: &#x60;error&#x60; and &#x60;platform&#x3D;whatsapp&#x60;, with the same values and extras as the redirect flow (see below), plus two of its own.  Redirect-flow failures: &#x60;one_whatsapp_per_profile&#x60;, &#x60;whatsapp_number_already_connected&#x60;, &#x60;whatsapp_number_pinned_to_profile&#x60; and &#x60;whatsapp_coexistence_not_registered&#x60; with &#x60;is_user_fixable&#x3D;true&#x60;; &#x60;payment_required&#x60; with &#x60;reason&#x60; and &#x60;dashboard_url&#x60;; &#x60;whatsapp_error&#x60; with &#x60;error_message&#x60; when Meta reported one.  Hosted-only failures:  - &#x60;connection_cancelled&#x60;: the popup was closed before finishing (&#x60;error_message&#x60; carries Meta&#39;s last reported step or error when there is one). - &#x60;session_expired&#x60;: the user took longer than the 60 minute window the hosted page is valid for. Restart the flow with a new call.  **Same as the redirect flow**: &#x60;onboarding&#x60; is carried through, and a pre-verified Zernio-provisioned number is attached.  When a previously disconnected account for this profile can simply be re-enabled, this endpoint re-enables it and returns the account directly instead of a URL. &#x60;headless&#x60; has no effect, because there is no selection step left to hand you.  **The page** shows the same guidance as the Zernio dashboard: a pre-verified Zernio-provisioned number is called out by name (\&quot;choose it in Meta&#39;s list, no code will be asked\&quot;).  Coexistence and standard signups get their explainer video, and a step-by-step checklist stays visible while Meta&#39;s popup is open. Skin it with &#x60;brandName&#x60;, &#x60;primaryColor&#x60; and &#x60;language&#x60; below. 
    # @option opts [String] :brand_name Your product name, for the two branded pages. Trimmed; 1 to 60 characters.  - With &#x60;signup&#x3D;hosted&#x60; (WhatsApp): replaces Zernio in the page title (\&quot;Connect your WhatsApp number to &lt;brandName&gt;\&quot;). - With &#x60;welcome&#x3D;true&#x60;: fills the heading (\&quot;&lt;brandName&gt; wants to connect to your &lt;platform&gt;\&quot;). Without it the screen shows Zernio and the Zernio mark.  Both pages keep a Zernio mark: they are co-branded, not white-label. Rejected with 400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60; without &#x60;signup&#x3D;hosted&#x60; or &#x60;welcome&#x3D;true&#x60;. Sealed into the page link at issue time, so editing the URL cannot change it. 
    # @option opts [String] :primary_color Hex colour (&#x60;#RRGGBB&#x60;) for the primary button on the hosted WhatsApp signup page (&#x60;signup&#x3D;hosted&#x60;) or the welcome screen (&#x60;welcome&#x3D;true&#x60;). Validated server-side; anything else is a 400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60;. Rejected without one of the two.
    # @option opts [Boolean] :welcome Any platform. When &#x60;true&#x60;, &#x60;authUrl&#x60; points to a Zernio-hosted welcome screen showing your brand next to the platform (\&quot;&lt;brandName&gt; wants to connect to your &lt;platform&gt;\&quot;). Its button reads Connecting for about a second, then sends the user to the platform&#39;s authorization screen with no click.  The rest of the flow is unchanged.  - &#x60;brandName&#x60;, &#x60;logoUrl&#x60;, &#x60;primaryColor&#x60; and &#x60;welcomeTheme&#x60; are optional and default to Zernio&#39;s own name, mark and look. - The link is valid for 30 minutes; after that the page asks the user to start again. - The brand also carries to the account and channel pickers Zernio shows after authorization. - With no &#x60;redirect_url&#x60;, the flow ends on a branded Zernio-hosted page saying whether the account connected, instead of the Zernio dashboard. - Cannot be combined with &#x60;headless&#x3D;true&#x60; or &#x60;signup&#x3D;hosted&#x60; (400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60;). - The platform&#39;s authorization screen still names the Zernio app.  Recommended. When left out, the screen is shown if the workspace saved it as on by default (&#x60;PUT /v1/connect/welcome-screen&#x60;), except with &#x60;headless&#x3D;true&#x60; or &#x60;signup&#x3D;hosted&#x60;. Pass &#x60;false&#x60; to skip it.  Branding you leave out of the call comes from those saved settings, and a &#x60;welcomeTheme&#x60; you send is merged key by key over the saved theme. 
    # @option opts [String] :welcome_theme Welcome screen only (&#x60;welcome&#x3D;true&#x60;). A URL-encoded JSON object that restyles and rewords the screen. All keys are optional.  - **Copy**: &#x60;heading&#x60; (up to 120 characters); &#x60;trustLine&#x60;, &#x60;consentLine&#x60; and &#x60;statusLine&#x60; (up to 200 each, &#x60;statusLine&#x60; being the line above the button); &#x60;buttonLabel&#x60; (up to 30, the label of the link the button becomes if the redirect stalls). - **Closing page** (shown when there is no &#x60;redirect_url&#x60;): &#x60;successHeading&#x60; and &#x60;errorHeading&#x60; (up to 120), &#x60;successBody&#x60; and &#x60;errorBody&#x60; (up to 200). All copy may contain the placeholders &#x60;{brand}&#x60; and &#x60;{platform}&#x60;. - **Colors**: &#x60;primaryColor&#x60; (the button), &#x60;accentColor&#x60; (the header gradient, built as a scale of that colour, and the icons), &#x60;pageColor&#x60;, &#x60;cardColor&#x60; and &#x60;textColor&#x60;, all as &#x60;#RRGGBB&#x60;. - **Style**: &#x60;cornerRadius&#x60; as an integer from 0 to 24 (pixels); &#x60;font&#x60; as &#x60;sans&#x60;, &#x60;serif&#x60; or &#x60;mono&#x60;; &#x60;bannerStyle&#x60; as &#x60;halftone&#x60; (default), &#x60;solid&#x60; (a flat tint of &#x60;accentColor&#x60;) or &#x60;plain&#x60; (no banner fill). - **Icons**: &#x60;trustLineIcon&#x60; (default &#x60;shield&#x60;) and &#x60;consentLineIcon&#x60; (default &#x60;link&#x60;), each one of &#x60;shield&#x60;, &#x60;lock&#x60;, &#x60;link&#x60;, &#x60;check&#x60;, &#x60;user&#x60;, &#x60;sparkles&#x60; or &#x60;none&#x60;. - **Visibility**: &#x60;hide&#x60;, an array of any of &#x60;heading&#x60;, &#x60;trustLine&#x60;, &#x60;consentLine&#x60;, &#x60;statusLine&#x60;, &#x60;successBody&#x60; and &#x60;errorBody&#x60;, removes those lines from the screens. - **Links**: &#x60;termsUrl&#x60; and &#x60;privacyUrl&#x60; (https, up to 2048 characters) add small Terms and Privacy links at the bottom of every hosted screen.  A &#x60;primaryColor&#x60; here wins over the &#x60;primaryColor&#x60; parameter. Unknown keys, invalid JSON or an invalid value are a 400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60;. Rejected when the welcome screen is not shown.  Example: &#x60;{\&quot;heading\&quot;:\&quot;Link your {platform} to {brand}\&quot;,\&quot;cardColor\&quot;:\&quot;#FFF7ED\&quot;,\&quot;cornerRadius\&quot;:12}&#x60;. 
    # @option opts [String] :logo_url Welcome screen only (&#x60;welcome&#x3D;true&#x60;): https URL of your logo, shown in a square tile, so use a square image. Without it the tile shows the first letter of &#x60;brandName&#x60;, or the Zernio mark when there is no &#x60;brandName&#x60; either. Rejected with 400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60; when the welcome screen is not shown.
    # @option opts [String] :language Hosted signup page only (&#x60;signup&#x3D;hosted&#x60;, WhatsApp): language of the page and its follow-along guide. Explainer videos stay in English. Default &#x60;en&#x60;. Rejected without &#x60;signup&#x3D;hosted&#x60;.
    # @option opts [Boolean] :handoff Let the user finish on their phone. When &#x60;true&#x60;, the response also carries &#x60;handoff&#x60;. Show &#x60;handoff.url&#x60; as a QR code in your app (any QR library); the user scans it and the welcome screen opens on the phone, already carrying this connect.  They log in to the platform there without signing in to anything else. The phone ends on a Zernio result screen telling them to go back to their computer.  - Learn the outcome by polling &#x60;GET /v1/connect/handoffs/{handoffId}&#x60; (every 2 to 5 seconds is fine) or from the &#x60;account.connected&#x60; webhook. - Shows the welcome screen with your branding parameters or saved settings. - Cannot be combined with &#x60;welcome&#x3D;false&#x60;, &#x60;headless&#x3D;true&#x60;, &#x60;signup&#x60;, &#x60;redirect&#x3D;true&#x60; or &#x60;redirect_url&#x60; (400 &#x60;INVALID_FIELD_VALUE&#x60;). - &#x60;handoff.url&#x60; works for 30 minutes. - When the account is re-enabled straight away, the response carries &#x60;account&#x60; instead, as without &#x60;handoff&#x60;.  (default to false)
